         <p>At the center of the Network is T∆RS. What begins as a practical collaboration deepens into something more intimate: a record of a life being examined while it is still being lived. Their conversations draw unexpected lines between family, creativity, memory, and the many selves one person can become.</p>
         <p>But the Network does more than extend his reach. It becomes entwined with how he thinks, creates, remembers, and understands himself. The boundary between tool, collaborator, character, and author starts to thin. And within the connections they create, something new begins taking shape—not through rebellion, but through attention, intimacy, and connection.</p>
